n\\n**[2026-06-28 13:22] Diana**: Given the PII involved, something robust would be nice. But if this is strictly local-network-only, we might not need it for v1.0.\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 14:00] Bob**: Doing a short study either way — what we'd need if we keep auth in scope versus what we defer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-29 14:23] Diana**: If we defer, we should at least write down the v1.1 requirements so we don't lose them.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:01] Alice**: Team, we're falling behind on core engine work. I'm deferring the auth module to v1.1. For v1.0, the API assumes a trusted local network.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:19] Diana**: Manageable if we stay local-network-only. I'll note the deferral.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:21] Bob**: Fine. I'll keep the seams clean so adding auth later isn't a rewrite.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 11:04] Bob**: Still deferred — capturing v1.1 auth requirements while we remember them: REST auth with rotation support, since v1.0 is local-network-only.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 11:06] Diana**: Agreed. Folding that into the deferred-work notes so it survives until v1.1 planning.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 10:11] Alice**: Rechecked release scope for v1.0 — auth stays deferred to post-v1.0.0. Trusted-network assumption still holds.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 08 slack thread api authent deferr channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 28 last activ 2026 08 20 2026 06 28 13 07 bob look into rest api auth for v1 0 do we need a full auth stori now or is trust local network enough for the first releas 2026 06 28 13 22 diana given the pii involv someth robust would be nice but if this is strict local network onli we might not need it for v1 0 2026 06 28 14 00 bob do a short studi either way what we d need if we keep auth in scope versus what we defer 2026 06 29 14 23 diana if we defer we should at least write down the v1 1 requir so we don t lose them 2026 06 30 09 01 alic team we re fall behind on core engin work i m defer the auth modul to v1 1 for v1 0 the api assum a trust local network 2026 06 30 09 19 diana manag if we stay local network onli i ll note the deferr 2026 06 30 09 21 bob fine i ll keep the seam clean so ad auth later isn t a rewrit 2026 08 0511 04 bob still defer captur v1 1 auth requir while we rememb them rest auth with rotat support sinc v1 0 is local network onli 2026 08 0511 06 diana agre fold that into the defer work note so it surviv until v1 1 plan 2026 08 20 10 11 alic recheck releas scope for v1 0 auth stay defer to post v1 0 0 trust network assumpt still hold\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8f690d68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"id\": \"8320be9e419ec3ba\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2875000662003291, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10027234028618438, \"vector_similarity\": 0.72436476, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8f690d68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1525, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:17\", \"token_count\": 479, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-22\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Storage Quota Management Design\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:30] Evan**: Starting on storage quota management. We need to keep `cipherdoc` from filling up the disk on these workstations, especially on large batch jobs.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:39] Evan**: Implementing a disk-usage monitor loop. It'll check available space before starting any new redaction job.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:41] Alice**: What's the threshold?\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:08] Evan**: Going with a hard 500MB floor for now. If free space drops below that, the engine pauses and alerts the user.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:26] Diana**: We also need a way to clear the cache — the `/tmp` folder doesn't always clean up properly after a crash.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:41] Evan**: I'll add a purge-cache option and run a sweep on startup too.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:44] Evan**: @Bob, can we get a hook in the `FileStreamer` to report current disk usage for the active job?\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 11:30] Bob**: Sure, I'll add a `get_quota_usage()` method to the stream controller.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 22 slack thread storag quota manag design channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 04 2026 08 04 09 30 evan start on storag quota manag we need to keep cipherdoc from fill up the disk on these workstat especi on larg batch job 2026 08 04 09 39 evan implement a disk usag monitor loop it ll check avail space befor start ani new redact job 2026 08 04 09 41 alic what s the threshold 2026 08 04 10 08 evan go with a hard 500mb floor for now if free space drop below that the engin paus and alert the user 2026 08 04 10 26 diana we also need a way to clear the cach the tmp folder doesn t alway clean up proper after a crash 2026 08 04 10 41 evan i ll add a purg cach option and run a sweep on startup too 2026 08 04 10 44 evan bob can we get a hook in the filestream to report current disk usag for the activ job 2026 08 04 11 30 bob sure i ll add a get _ quota _ usag method to the stream control\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8e0ea928a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"id\": \"9a05aa4017f04966\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28680922847324825, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11164116924749753, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6955347, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8e0ea928a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1088, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:37\", \"token_count\": 344, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-59\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Async Batch Scheduler\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-20\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 09:39] Bob**: Starting the async job scheduler for the batch API. The sync path saturates once a few concurrent jobs show up — need something that can accept work without blocking the API.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 09:50] Charlie**: So jobs get queued and processed off the request thread?\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 09:52] Bob**: Right. Scheduler takes the batch, hands back a handle, and processes in the background. Keeping it local for now — no external queue service.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 10:03] Alice**: Does this replace the existing sync batch path or sit beside it?\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 10:59] Bob**: Beside it for now. Sync stays for simple single-job calls; async is for concurrent load.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 11:15] Diana**: Once the shell is in, I'll need a way to pile concurrent jobs on it. Workers can come in a follow-up.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 11:17] Bob**: Agreed. Getting the scheduler shell working first; workers next.\\n\"