6 08 21 keyboard pas diana exercis keyboard navig on the preview surfac and move the task to activ a screen reader trial wa plan a a later step in the same audit and is not document here sourc id src gdoc 33 access find keyboard pas on preview owner diana document key doc 2033 last updat 2026 09 08 retrospect cover 2026 08 21 t039 open a an access audit of ui surfac the first concret step wa keyboard navig on the redact preview so review can move through preview control without a point devic supersess on 2026 08 24 alic supersed the a11y audit the complet visual preview overlay overhaul t023 wa judg to alreadi cover the style and access scope this task track the keyboard pas find therefor did not continu a a standalon a11y workstream\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9da74908a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-08-Accessibility-a11y-Audit-Review.md\", \"id\": \"dbbb35710d0c00e8\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28371549640610433, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11508959200872047, \"vector_similarity\": 0.67717594, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-08-Accessibility-a11y-Audit-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9da74908a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-08-Accessibility-a11y-Audit-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-08-Accessibility-a11y-Audit-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 892, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:06\", \"token_count\": 322, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"*Note*: Do not treat the async queue as production-stable until the manifest-write race is fixed and the ~10% throughput regression is recovered.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"note do not treat the async queue a product stabl until the manifest write race is fix and the 10 throughput regress is recov\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9a578b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"id\": \"fd285c4f6471561e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2833500251331851, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10372076304740734, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70248497, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9a578b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1694, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:51\", \"token_count\": 573, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-06\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Docker Image Size Optimization\\n\\n**Channel**: #releases\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-25\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-25 09:35] Diana**: @Evan, I just pulled the latest `cipherdoc` image. It's 2.1GB! That's way too big for a local runtime deployment. Reopening the Docker packaging task.\\n\\n**[2026-08-01 09:30] Evan**: Whoa, 2.1GB, and we still haven't closed out the CVE verification either. Looks like the full Ubuntu base is a big part of the bloat. I'll put together a multi-stage build plan targeting somewhere around 450MB.\\n\\n**[2026-08-01 09:33] Diana**: That'd get it onto standard dev laptops without eating all the disk space. Let's aim for that.\\n\\n**[2026-08-01 10:04] Evan**: Multi-stage build plan is in place. Stripping out the build-time dependencies from the final artifact.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 13:11] Evan**: The multi-stage split alone still leaves the base layer too large. Swapping from `ubuntu:22.04` to `alpine:latest` as the base. Had some issues with `glibc` vs `musl`, but `gcompat` seems to fix it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 15:21] Evan**: Alpine swap didn't get us all the way there either. Just removed the unused OCR and runtime packages we aren't shipping in this build.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:00] Diana**: Checked the size and ran the CVE scan. We're still over the ~450MB target, and the CVE verification is still failing.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:10] Evan**: Yeah, not where we need to be yet. There's still fluff in the Python site-packages layer, and I need to chase down what's tripping the CVE scan.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:13] Diana**: Reopened status stands until both the size and the CVE check are clean. I'll keep tracking it against the release checklist.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 06 slack thread docker imag size optim channel releas thread open 2026 06 25 last activ 2026 08 12 2026 06 25 09 35 diana evan i just pull the latest cipherdoc imag it s2 1gb that s way too big for a local runtim deploy reopen the docker packag task 2026 0801 09 30 evan whoa 2 1gb and we still haven t close out the cve verif either look like the full ubuntu base is a big part of the bloat i ll put togeth a multi stage build plan target somewher around 450mb 2026 0801 09 33 diana that d get it onto standard dev laptop without eat all the disk space let s aim for that 2026 0801 1004 evan multi stage build plan is in place strip out the build time depend from the final artifact 2026 08 04 13 11 evan the multi stage split alon still leaf the base layer too larg swap from ubuntu 22 04 to alpin latest a the base had some issu with glibc v musl but gcompat seem to fix it 2026 08 07 15 21 evan alpin swap didn t get u all the way there either just remov the unus ocr and runtim packag we aren t ship in this build 2026 08 12 09 00 diana check the size and ran the cve scan we re still over the 450mb target and the cve verif is still fail 2026 08 12 09 10 evan yeah not where we need to be yet there s still fluff in the python site packag layer and i need to chase down what s trip the cve scan 2026 08 12 09 13 diana reopen status stand until both the size and the cve check are clean i ll keep track it against the releas checklist\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8ee6a5a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-25-docker-size.md\", \"id\": \"87fb525087edc8d4\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2827057984732483, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11164116924749753, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6818566, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-25-docker-size.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8ee6a5a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-25-docker-size.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-25-docker-size.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1720, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:24\", \"token_count\": 513, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-21\\n\\n# Slack Thread: AES-256 Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:20] Bob**: Moving forward with the AES-256 pipeline now that the crypto eval settled on it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:28] Bob**: Merged it — every temp file in the processing queue is now encrypted with a per-session key.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:37] Diana**: Running a stress test. What happens if the system loses power mid-redaction? Does the encrypted temp file persist?\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:38] Bob**: Yes, but it's useless without the session key, which only lives in volatile memory. On reboot, the cleanup hook wipes it anyway.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:39] Diana**: Makes sense.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:23] Diana**: Crypto sign-off done. Verified the `/tmp/cipherdoc` data is unreadable without the session key.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:41] Diana**: This also builds on the fail-closed work — the pipeline integrates with that deletion behavior cleanly.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:43] Bob**: Calling this done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:44] Alice**: Nice. :white_check_mark:\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 21 slack thread ae 256 encrypt pipelin channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 05 last activ 2026 08 07 2026 08 05 09 20 bob move forward with the ae 256 pipelin now that the crypto eval settl on it 2026 08 05 09 28 bob merg it everi temp file in the process queue is now encrypt with a per session key 2026 08 05 09 37 diana run a stress test what happen if the system lose power mid redact doe the encrypt temp file persist 2026 08 05 09 38 bob yes but it s useless without the session key which onli life in volatil memori on reboot the cleanup hook wipe it anyway 2026 08 05 09 39 diana make sens 2026 08 07 13 23 diana crypto sign off done verifi the tmp cipherdoc data is unread without the session key 2026 08 07 13 41 diana this also build on the fail close work the pipelin integr with that delet behavior clean 2026 08 07 13 43 bob call this done 2026 08 07 13 44 alic nice white _ check _ mark\",