\", \"size\": 1051, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:35\", \"token_count\": 566, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-44\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Large File Chunking Merge\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-16\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-20\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 09:19] Charlie**: Merged the stream-chunking implementation into mainline. Calling this done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 09:21] Alice**: Great, this was overdue. Nice work.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 09:57] Bob**: Anything left over from the memory concerns during testing, or is it fully clean?\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 10:00] Charlie**: As far as testing showed, clean. We'll see if anything shows up on longer runs.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 09:01] Charlie**: Following up on the leak Bob found on the larger files — root cause was the chunk buffers not being explicitly released once a worker moved past them. Refactoring the buffer-release path now.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 09:15] Bob**: Does the fix release eagerly after each chunk, or wait until the whole file finishes?\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 09:18] Charlie**: Eagerly, right after each chunk is processed — that's the whole point, don't let it accumulate. Still working through it, not ready to call it done again yet.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 09:51] Diana**: Let me know when there's a build to re-run the stress case against.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 44 slack thread larg file chunk merg channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 16 last activ 2026 08 20 2026 08 16 09 19 charli merg the stream chunk implement into mainlin call this done 2026 08 16 09 21 alic great this wa overdu nice work 2026 08 16 09 57 bob anyth left over from the memori concern dure test or is it fulli clean 2026 08 16 1000 charli a far a test show clean we ll see if anyth show up on longer run 2026 08 20 09 01 charli follow up on the leak bob found on the larger file root caus wa the chunk buffer not be explicit releas onc a worker move past them refactor the buffer releas path now 2026 08 20 09 15 bob doe the fix releas eager after each chunk or wait until the whole file finish 2026 08 20 09 18 charli eager right after each chunk is process that s the whole point don t let it accumul still work through it not readi to call it done again yet 2026 08 20 09 51 diana let me know when there s a build to re run the stress case against\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8eb3f568a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-large-file-chunking-merge.md\", \"id\": \"eff9d8093fd3e4c5\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2925238667439957, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1104287382057082, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7174125, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-large-file-chunking-merge.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8eb3f568a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-large-file-chunking-merge.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-large-file-chunking-merge.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1195, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:27\", \"token_count\": 363, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Opt-Out Behaviour Designed\\n\\nThe CLI and API collect anonymous usage metrics (pages processed, OCR fallback rate) to help tune the detection engine. Setting `CIPHER_TELEMETRY=0`, or the equivalent GUI toggle, is designed to immediately stop all outbound telemetry traffic to the metrics endpoint.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Design-Time Issue Found and Patched: Pending-Queue Leak\\n\\nWhile designing the flag semantics, testing surfaced that the opt-out flag blocked network egress correctly, but the `TelemetryLogger` kept writing event payloads to a local SQLite queue regardless. That meant re-enabling telemetry later would flush the entire backlog accumulated during the opt-out period, including events the user believed were never being recorded. The logger was patched to a no-op backend when opted out, closing that gap before the flag semantics were finalized.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Verification (Retrospective)\\n\\nA network trace on 2026-08-24 confirmed zero outbound telemetry traffic once the opt-out flag is set, closing the CLI-side verification as Completed.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Remaining Limitation\\n\\nThe third-party Electron crash reporter (Sentry) has not been audited for whether it independently respects the opt-out environment variable or requires its own disable hook for minidump uploads.\\n\\n*Note*: CLI-side telemetry opt-out is verified. Full privacy compliance for air-gapped/opt-out users cannot be claimed until the Sentry crash-reporter path is audited separately.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 opt out behaviour design the cli and api collect anonym usag metric page process ocr fallback rate to help tune the detect engin set cipher _ telemetri 0 or the equival gui toggl is design to immedi stop all outbound telemetri traffic to the metric endpoint sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 design time issu found and patch pend queue leak while design the flag semant test surfac that the opt out flag block network egress correct but the telemetrylogg kept write event payload to a local sqlite queue regardless that meant re enabl telemetri later would flush the entir backlog accumul dure the opt out period includ event the user believ were never be record the logger wa patch to a no op backend when opt out close that gap befor the flag semant were final sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 verif retrospect a network trace on 2026 08 24 confirm zero outbound telemetri traffic onc the opt out flag is set close the cli side verif a complet sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 remain limit the third parti electron crash report sentri ha not been audit for whether it independ respect the opt out environ variabl or requir it own disabl hook for minidump upload note cli side telemetri opt out is verifi full privaci complianc for air gap opt out user can not be claim until the sentri crash report path is audit separ\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9e43bb08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"id\": \"c3381a6a564a6c9c\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2911603594061043, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11508959200872047, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70199215, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9e43bb08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1587, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:00:54\", \"token_count\": 503, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- **2026-09-18**: Bob - Buffer Refactor (Active (Reopened))\\n\\n - *Refactored the disk-usage monitor to allow a 10% buffer above quota, since the reopened hard halt was tripping too aggressively on production-like batches.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"2026 09 18 bob buffer refactor activ reopen refactor the disk usag monitor to allow a 10 buffer abov quota sinc the reopen hard halt wa trip too aggress on product like batch\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e95b620e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-32-Storage-Quota-Management.md\", \"id\": \"35710838c33b7c79\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29089613440610435, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11508959200872047, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7011114, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-32-Storage-Quota-Management.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\