he redact polici configur implement\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e98ff9a68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-16-Redaction-Policy-Config.md\", \"id\": \"67615f6af041edac\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2821790683346169, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09337549476373849, \"vector_similarity\": 0.72272074, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-16-Redaction-Policy-Config.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e98ff9a68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-16-Redaction-Policy-Config.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-16-Redaction-Policy-Config.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 905, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:08\", \"token_count\": 494, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-32\\n\\n# Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2032\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective decision note on the opt-out flag semantics settled 2026-08-20 for CIPH-48 (Telemetry Opt-Out).\\n\\n## Decision\\n\\nThe CLI accepts an explicit `--no-telemetry` flag. When present, it must suppress every outbound telemetry call for that invocation, including startup pings and error reports — not just usage-metric events.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-32\\n\\n# Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2032\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective decision note on the opt-out flag semantics settled 2026-08-20 for CIPH-48 (Telemetry Opt-Out).\\n\\n## Why \\\"explicit\\\" matters\\n\\nThe flag was deliberately specified as opt-out rather than opt-in-by-default-off, since the goal was to give privacy-sensitive users a clear, discoverable switch rather than relying on a config file most users would never find.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-32\\n\\n# Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2032\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective decision note on the opt-out flag semantics settled 2026-08-20 for CIPH-48 (Telemetry Opt-Out).\\n\\n## Note\\n\\nThis record settles the flag's expected behavior. Confirming that behavior against an actual network trace was a separate verification step and is not part of this decision note.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 32 telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2032 last updat 2026 09 06 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect decis note on the opt out flag semant settl 2026 08 20 for ciph 48 telemetri opt out decis the cli accept an explicit no telemetri flag when present it must suppress everi outbound telemetri call for that invoc includ startup ping and error report not just usag metric event sourc id src gdoc 32 telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2032 last updat 2026 09 06 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect decis note on the opt out flag semant settl 2026 08 20 for ciph 48 telemetri opt out whi explicit matter the flag wa deliber specifi a opt out rather than opt in by default off sinc the goal wa to give privaci sensit user a clear discover switch rather than reli on a config file most user would never find sourc id src gdoc 32 telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2032 last updat 2026 09 06 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect decis note on the opt out flag semant settl 2026 08 20 for ciph 48 telemetri opt out note this record settl the flag s expect behavior confirm that behavior against an actual network trace wa a separ verif step and is not part of this decis note\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9a043428a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"id\": \"af63545a0d15b5f6\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2819444344061043, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11508959200872047, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6712724, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9a043428a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 947, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:55\", \"token_count\": 416, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-05\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Offset Mismatch Debugging\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-06-23\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 08:56] Charlie**: @Diana, I'm seeing weird behavior in the test cases. The redaction masks are shifted by a character or two in some PDF exports.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 09:01] Diana**: Multi-column layouts? I told you pdfminer output was injecting spaces.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 09:43] Charlie**: It's not just the spaces. The engine sees the text at one offset, but the PDF coordinates are different after the cleaning phase.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 10:51] Diana**: Are you seeing this on all viewers? Sometimes Acrobat renders overlays differently than Chrome's PDF viewer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 10:52] Charlie**: Looking at the raw coordinate output for now. Whitespace normalization looks like the culprit — non-breaking spaces keep showing up in the extracted text.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 10:53] Charlie**: Still stuck. Tried mapping cleaned offsets back to raw ones, but the math falls apart on dense pages.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 12:40] Diana**: Can we get most of the standard text aligned and park the edge cases?\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 12:42] Charlie**: Not really — on dense docs it's closer to half the spans. Starting to look like an upstream pdfminer.six issue. I'm going to check their tracker.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 12:45] Alice**: Status?\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 12:47] Charlie**: No. Offline tonight.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 05 slack thread offset mismatch debug channel cipherdoc date 2026 06 23 2026 06 23 08 56 charli diana i m see weird behavior in the test case the redact mask are shift by a charact or two in some pdf export 2026 06 23 09 01 diana multi column layout i told you pdfminer output wa inject space 2026 06 23 09 43 charli it s not just the space the engin see the text at one offset but the pdf coordin are differ after the clean phase 2026 06 23 10 51 diana are you see this on all viewer sometim acrobat render overlay differ than chrome s pdf viewer 2026 06 23 10 52 charli look at the raw coordin output for now whitespac normal look like the culprit non break space keep show up in the extract text 2026 06 23 10 53 charli still stuck tri map clean offset back to raw one but the math fall apart on dens page 2026 06 23 12 40 diana can we get most of the standard text align and park the edg case 2026 06 23 12 42 charli not realli on dens doc it s closer to half the span start to look like an upstream pdfminer six issu i m go to check their tracker 2026 06 23 12 45 alic status 2026 06 23 12 47 charli no offlin tonight\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e938a76e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-23-offset-bug-debug.md\", \"id\": \"feb7b0bf42cb1a60\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.27890041406169774, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08200666580242535, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73831916, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-23-offset-bug-debug.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e938a76e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-23-offset-bug-debug.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-23-offset-bug-debug.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1387, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:24\", \"token_count\": 405, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-03\\n\\n# Slack Thread: REST API Scaffolding and TempFile Policy\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-06-14\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 09:09] Bob**: Starting on the REST API scaffolding. Going with FastAPI for the layer. It's lightweight and the auto-generated OpenAPI docs will save us a ton of time.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 09:39] Diana**: +1 for FastAPI. Can we ensure we have request validation schemas for the upload endpoint? We don't want malformed JSON crashing the engine.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 09:43] Bob**: Already on it. Using Pydantic for the `RedactionRequest` model. Scaffold is up and running in the `api-scaffold` branch.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 10:50] Bob**: Quick update on the file handling. I'm implementing a strict temp-file cleanup policy.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 10:56] Diana**: How are we handling cleanup? If a request fails mid-stream, do we leave orphaned files on the container?\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 11:15] Bob**: No, I'm using a `try...finally` block with a context manager. Files are wiped immediately after the redaction job completes or errors out. No PII should ever persist in `/tmp`.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 11:16] Diana**: What about memory-mapped files for larger uploads?\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 11:33] Bob**: For now, everything is streamed. We might need `mmap` later, but for the MVP, the context manager approach is safer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 11:47] Diana**: I'll start the security audit once you merge the policy. We need to be 100% sure about that cleanup logic.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 03 slack thread rest api scaffold and tempfil polici channel cipherdoc date 2026 06 14 2026 06 14 09 09 bob start on the rest api scaffold go with fastapi for the layer it s lightweight and the auto generat openapi doc will save u a ton of time 2026 06 14 09 39 diana 1 for fastapi can we ensur we have request valid schema for the upload endpoint we don t want malform json crash the engin 2026 06 14 09 43 bob alreadi on it use pydant for the redactionrequest model scaffold is up and run in the api scaffold branch 2026 06 14 10 50 bob quick updat on the file handl i m implement a strict temp file cleanup polici 2026 06 14 10 56 diana how are we handl cleanup if a request fail mid stream do we leav orphan file on the contain 2026 06 14 11 15 bob no i m use a tri final block with a context manag file are wipe immedi after the redact job complet or error out no pii should ever persist in tmp 2026 06 14 11 16 diana what about memori map file for larger upload 2026 06 14 11 33 bob for now everyth is stream we might need mmap later but for the mvp the context manag approach is safer 2026 06 14 11 47 diana i ll start the secur audit onc you merg the polici we need to be 100 sure about that cleanup logic\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8f9c6b68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-14-api-endpoint.md\", \"id\": \"69a1fcec04db9683\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.27787984633461693, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09337549476373849, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70839, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-14-api-endpoint.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8f9c6b68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-14-api-endpoint.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-14-api-endpoint.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1463, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:13\", \"token_count\": 436, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-17\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Offline Auth Mock and Rotation Block\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:14] Bob**: Building the local auth mock for air-gap testing so we can exercise Diana's key-rotation design without a real deployment.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:16] Bob**: Mock is up. It runs the rotation flow with the network disabled, same as a real air-gapped site would see.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:27] Diana**: Good, that's exactly what I need to validate the design against.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 08:36] Alice**: How'd it go?\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 08:45] Bob**: Not great. Key rotation just can't complete with the network down — the flow we designed assumes at least a brief connection to finish the handshake.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 08:48] Alice**: Ugh.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:13] Diana**: So we're blocked. There's no resolution yet on how to rotate without any network at all.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:33] Alice**: Offline auth stays blocked. Let's regroup on whether the design needs to change or whether we relax the offline requirement.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 17 slack thread offlin auth mock and rotat block channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 04 last activ 2026 08 05 2026 08 04 09 14 bob build the local auth mock for air gap test so we can exercis diana s key rotat design without a real deploy 2026 08 04 09 16 bob mock is up it run the rotat flow with the network disabl same a a real air gap site would see 2026 08 04 10 27 diana good that s exact what i need to valid the design against 2026 08 05 08 36 alic how d it go 2026 08 05 08 45 bob not great key rotat just can t complet with the network down the flow we design assum at least a brief connect to finish the handshak 2026 08 05 08 48 alic ugh 2026 08 05 09 13 diana so we re block there s no resolut yet on how to rotat without ani network at all 2026 08 05 09 33 alic offlin auth stay block let s regroup on whether the design need to chang or whether we relax the offlin requir\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8cb8e688a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-offline-auth-mock-block.md\", \"id\": \"0d5f3fc5f1872d47\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.27769556606169776, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08200666580242535, \"vector_similarity\": 0.734303, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-offline-auth-mock-block.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8cb8e688a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-offline-auth-mock-block.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-offline-auth-mock-block.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1092, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:54\", \"token_count\": 340, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-46\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Redaction Profile Export API\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-14\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 09:23] Bob**: Hey @engine, just pushed the initial implementation for the export API. You can hit `/v1/export/profile` on the dev branch now. It should return the full Pydantic-validated policy bundle.\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 09:28] Charlie**: Nice. Does it include the regex manifest, or is that a separate call? I need to know what patterns were active for the audit trail.\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 09:46] Bob**: It's all in the one bundle. I've got a `regex_manifest` key that maps the pattern IDs to the actual compiled strings and their internal tags.\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 09:57] Alice**: @Bob will this export include the user-defined overrides too? We had that discussion in the standup about making sure manual reviewers can see why a rule was bypassed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 09:59] Bob**: Yeah, the `overrides` list is included. It's basically a JSON dump of the current state of the profile.\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 10:36] Diana**: Just pulled the latest and tried hitting it with an uninitialized profile. It's returning a 500 right now instead of a 404. I'll open a sub-task, but Bob can you look at the null check on the `profile_manager`?\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 10:39] Bob**: My bad, I see it. The session wasn't being validated before the export call. Pushing a fix to `feature/export-api` in 5 mins. :pinched_fingers:\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 10:41] Diana**: Fixed! Returning 404 now for empty states. :thumbsup:\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 46 slack thread redact profil export api channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 14 2026 08 14 09 23 bob hey engin just push the initi implement for the export api you can hit v1 export profil on the dev branch now it should return the full pydant valid polici bundl 2026 08 14 09 28 charli nice doe it includ the regex manifest or is that a separ call i need to know what pattern were activ for the audit trail 2026 08 14 09 46 bob it s all in the one bundl i ve got a regex _ manifest key that map the pattern id to the actual compil string and their intern tag 2026 08 14 09 57 alic bob will this export includ the user defin overrid too we had that discuss in the standup about make sure manual review can see whi a rule wa bypass 2026 08 14 09 59 bob yeah the overrid list is includ it s basic a json dump of the current state of the profil 2026 08 14 10 36 diana just pull the latest and tri hit it with an uniniti profil it s return a 500 right now instead of a 404 i ll open a sub task but bob can you look at the null check on the profil _ manag 2026 08 14 10 39 bob my bad i see it the session wasn t be valid befor the export call push a fix to featur export api in 5 min pinch _ finger 2026 08 14 10 41 diana fix return 404 now for empti state thumbsup\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8dd842e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-redaction-profile-export-api.md\", \"id\": \"a0344269eb33520d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2774402863346169, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09337549476373849, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7069248, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-redaction-profile-export-api.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8dd842e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-redaction-profile-export-api.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-redaction-profile-export-api.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1509, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:39\", \"token_count\": 445, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-33\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Offline Batch Run\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 08:58] Diana**: Harness is ready, so I'm running a full batch through it with the network blocked at the OS level. Kicking off now.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 11:28] Diana**: Batch is still running clean — no unexpected outbound connection attempts logged so far.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 09:30] Diana**: Batch finished offline. Signing off, but flagging one thing: there's a roughly 45-second hang at startup where something in the licence check reaches for a remote endpoint before it gives up and falls back to the local path.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 09:42] Bob**: 45 seconds is a long time to sit there. Is that the encryption-pipeline license check?\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 10:54] Diana**: Looks that way — depends on the encryption work, so I'm not touching that path here. Recording it and moving on.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 10:56] Alice**: So we're calling this signed off?\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 11:08] Diana**: I'll close this out, but I want to be clear this is a preliminary offline pass — not a compliance certification. The 45-second hang is noted, not resolved.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 33 slack thread offlin batch run channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 08 last activ 2026 08 10 2026 08 08 08 58 diana har is readi so i m run a full batch through it with the network block at the o level kick off now 2026 08 08 11 28 diana batch is still run clean no unexpect outbound connect attempt log so far 2026 08 10 09 30 diana batch finish offlin sign off but flag one thing there s a rough 45 second hang at startup where someth in the licenc check reach for a remot endpoint befor it give up and fall back to the local path 2026 08 10 09 42 bob 45 second is a long time to sit there is that the encrypt pipelin licens check 2026 08 1010 54 diana look that way depend on the encrypt work so i m not touch that path here record it and move on 2026 08 1010 56 alic so we re call this sign off 2026 08 10 11 08 diana i ll close this out but i want to be clear this is a preliminari offlin pas not a complianc certif the 45 second hang is note not resolv\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9238f288a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-offline-batch-run.md\", \"id\": \"c04a1f0066314f5d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2769573560616977, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08200666580242535, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7318423, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-offline-batch-run.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9238f288a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-offline-batch-run.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-offline-batch-run.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1193, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:41\", \"token_count\": 353, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-60\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Async Batch Workers\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-22\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:21] Bob**: The async processing is looking good. I've integrated the progress callbacks so the GUI can show a real-time percentage.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:30] Diana**: I'm seeing some race conditions when two different users try to process the same file simultaneously. The lock isn't being released correctly.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:00] Bob**: Ah, I see it. I'm using the filename as the key in the lock manager, but not accounting for the user ID.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:02] Charlie**: Why not use the file hash instead? That way even if they have different filenames but it's the same content, we don't process it twice.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:12] Bob**: Good idea. I'll swap out the keys for the SHA-256 hash.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:17] Charlie**: Perfect.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:35] Alice**: @Bob how does this affect the multi-threading work Charlie did?\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 16:56] Bob**: They should play well together. The scheduler distributes the *files* to different workers, and each worker uses Charlie's multi-threaded engine to process the *internal* pages.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 60 slack thread async batch worker channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 22 2026 08 22 14 21 bob the async process is look good i ve integr the progress callback so the gui can show a real time percentag 2026 08 22 14 30 diana i m see some race condit when two differ user tri to process the same file simultan the lock isn t be releas correct 2026 08 22 15 00 bob ah i see it i m use the filenam a the key in the lock manag but not account for the user id 2026 08 22 15 02 charli whi not use the file hash instead that way even if they have differ filenam but it s the same content we don t process it twice 2026 08 22 15 12 bob good idea i ll swap out the key for the sha 256 hash 2026 08 22 15 17 charli perfect 2026 08 22 15 35 alic bob how doe this affect the multi thread work charli did 2026 08 22 16 56 bob they should play well togeth the schedul distribut the file to differ worker and each worker us charli s multi thread engin to process the intern page\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e903a1ae8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-async-batch-workers.md\", \"id\": \"238bec23f23e7682\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.27662273606169774, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08200666580242535, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7307269, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-async-batch-workers.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e903a1ae8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-async-batch-workers.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-async-batch-workers.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1171, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:05\", \"token_count\": 352, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-12\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Batch Failure Strategy (Fail-Closed)\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-12\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-07-16\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:09] Bob**: For the batch fail-closed question, we need to decide what happens if the engine crashes halfway through a 1,000-file batch. Do we keep the successful ones?\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:26] Charlie**: Absolutely not. If we can't guarantee 100% of the batch is safe, we should fail-closed. No partial exports.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:28] Bob**: Agreed. Drafting the plan now. If any worker node throws an unhandled exception, we abort the entire job and purge the output buffer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:43] Charlie**: I've added an exception hook to the core engine. It catches low-level segfaults and signals the controller to stop all active streams.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 11:23] Bob**: Implementation complete. Added an atomic rename step at the very end — the output folder stays empty until the last file is verified.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 12:53] Diana**: What about logs? We need to know *why* it failed.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:16] Bob**: Crash report gets written to a separate `audit_log.json` before the shutdown. Captures the stack trace and the filename that triggered the fault.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:17] Charlie**: Perfect. :lock:\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:19] Alice**: Thanks.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:30] Diana**: QA pass on fail-closed is done — confirmed no output file gets written on failure and the temp files get securely deleted. Signing off before the encryption and offline work start relying on this.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:31] Bob**: Calling this done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 12 slack thread batch failur strategi fail close channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 12 last activ 2026 07 16 2026 06 12 10 09 bob for the batch fail close question we need to decid what happen if the engin crash halfway through a1 000 file batch do we keep the success one 2026 06 12 10 26 charli absolut not if we can t guarante 100 of the batch is safe we should fail close no partial export 2026 06 12 10 28 bob agre draft the plan now if ani worker node throw an unhandl except we abort the entir job and purg the output buffer 2026 06 12 10 43 charli i ve ad an except hook to the core engin it catch low level segfault and signal the control to stop all activ stream 2026 06 12 11 23 bob implement complet ad an atom renam step at the veri end the output folder stay empti until the last file is verifi 2026 06 12 12 53 diana what about log we need to know whi it fail 2026 06 12 13 16 bob crash report get written to a separ audit _ log json befor the shutdown captur the stack trace and the filenam that trigger the fault 2026 06 12 13 17 charli perfect lock 2026 06 12 13 19 alic thank 2026 07 16 09 30 diana qa pas on fail close is done confirm no output file get written on failur and the temp file get secur delet sign off befor the encrypt and offlin work start reli on this 2026 07 16 09 31 bob call this done\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e906ce748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"id\": \"1313e24c5f4d4803\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2764704860616977, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08200666580242535, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7302194, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e906ce748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1616, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:03\", \"token_count\": 478, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Title**: Fix Coordinate/Offset Drift in Multi-Page PDFs\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-19\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-06-19**: Bob - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Task opened to investigate the coordinate/offset drift in multi-page PDF redaction.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"titl fix coordin offset drift in multi page pdfs status block assigne charli prioriti high date creat 2026 06 19 activ histori 2026 06 19 bob task creat open task open to investig the coordin offset drift in multi page pdf redact\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"do