he redaction pipeline (T010, WS-03). This report records findings as of the 2026-07-06 scan only; it is not a live task-status tracker.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-09\\n\\n# Redaction Pipeline — Security Scan Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2009\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-07-06\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\nThe 2026-07-06 scan flagged a medium-severity CORS misconfiguration: the API responds with `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`. That wildcard origin must be restricted before T010 can close. No patch has been applied as of this scan date.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-09\\n\\n# Redaction Pipeline — Security Scan Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2009\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-07-06\\n\\n## Status (as of 2026-07-06)\\n\\nActive — CORS finding handed to engineering for patching.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-09\\n\\n# Redaction Pipeline — Security Scan Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2009\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-07-06\\n\\n## Next Step\\n\\nAwait a CORS patch (restrict to configured `ALLOWED_ORIGINS`) and re-verification before this task moves to Completed. Later patch and re-scan outcomes are outside the scope of this dated scan report.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 09 redact pipelin secur scan report owner diana document key doc 2009 last updat 2026 07 06 scope secur audit of the redact pipelin t010 w 03 this report record find a of the 2026 07 06 scan onli it is not a live task status tracker sourc id src gdoc 09 redact pipelin secur scan report owner diana document key doc 2009 last updat 2026 07 06 find the 2026 07 06 scan flag a medium sever cor misconfigur the api respond with access control allow origin that wildcard origin must be restrict befor t010 can close no patch ha been appli a of this scan date sourc id src gdoc 09 redact pipelin secur scan report owner diana document key doc 2009 last updat 2026 07 06 status a of 2026 07 06 activ cor find hand to engin for patch sourc id src gdoc 09 redact pipelin secur scan report owner diana document key doc 2009 last updat 2026 07 06 next step await a cor patch restrict to configur allow _ origin and re verif befor this task move to complet later patch and re scan outcom are outsid the scope of this date scan report\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9e2a1d88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-06-Vulnerability-Scan.md\", \"id\": \"b20a1aa0db99edad\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.26666371778877856, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07063783684111222, \"vector_similarity\": 0.72405744, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-06-Vulnerability-Scan.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9e2a1d88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-06-Vulnerability-Scan.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-06-Vulnerability-Scan.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 867, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:00:56\", \"token_count\": 370, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-13\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Regex Flags Bug Discovery\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-07-09\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-07-09 08:56] Bob**: @Charlie, I found a discrepancy while running the CLI-API parity audit. The CLI is matching case-insensitive by default, but the REST API is case-sensitive for the same patterns.\\n\\n**[2026-07-09 09:11] Charlie**: That's a bug in how the `ConfigLoader` passes flags to the engine. It should be pulling the `ignore_case` bit from the YAML.\\n\\n**[2026-07-09 10:08] Bob**: Investigating now. Looks like the `RedactionRequest` Pydantic model in the API layer is defaulting `regex_flags` to 0 instead of reading the global config.\\n\\n**[2026-07-09 10:11] Bob**: Found it. PR #52 is up. I've standardized the flag inheritance so the API and CLI use the exact same initialization logic.\\n\\n**[2026-07-09 10:14] Charlie**: Nice catch. This would have caused some major headaches in production if some files were being missed because of casing.\\n\\n**[2026-07-09 10:51] Bob**: PR #52 merged and verified. I've added a test case to the parity suite that checks `NAME` vs `name` across both interfaces.\\n\\n**[2026-07-09 11:12] Diana**: Verified on my end too. Parity is holding up.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 13 slack thread regex flag bug discoveri channel cipherdoc date 2026 07 09 2026 07 09 08 56 bob charli i found a discrep while run the cli api pariti audit the cli is match case insensit by default but the rest api is case sensit for the same pattern 2026 07 09 09 11 charli that s a bug in how the configload pass flag to the engin it should be pull the ignor _ case bit from the yaml 2026 07 09 10 08 bob investig now look like the redactionrequest pydant model in the api layer is default regex _ flag to 0 instead of read the global config 2026 07 09 10 11 bob found it pr 52 is up i ve standard the flag inherit so the api and cli use the exact same initi logic 2026 07 09 10 14 charli nice catch this would have caus some major headach in product if some file were be miss becaus of case 2026 07 09 10 51 bob pr 52 merg and verifi i ve ad a test case to the pariti suit that check name v name across both interfac 2026 07 09 11 12 diana verifi on my end too pariti is hold up\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8f1bb748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-07-09-config-parity-discovery.md\", \"id\": \"b780ffe8ca4fa166\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2662795760616977, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08200666580242535, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6962497, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-07-09-config-parity-discovery.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8f1bb748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-07-09-config-parity-discovery.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-07-09-config-parity-discovery.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1208, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:20\", \"token_count\": 361, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-09\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Security Patch - CORS Issue\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-07-10\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-07-15\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:20] Diana**: @Bob, I just ran a security scan on the API. We've got a wide-open CORS policy. `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` is a no-go for this project.\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:23] Bob**: Oops, that was left over from local testing on the scaffold. I'll tighten it up now.\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:43] Bob**: Applying the CORS patch. It now only allows requests from the defined `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` in the environment config.\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:50] Diana**: Scan is coming back clean now.\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:52] Bob**: Thanks for the catch, Diana. I've added a lint check to prevent `*` from being committed in the future.\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 15:45] Alice**: Good catch. Let's make sure we don't have any other dev-only flags leaking into the main branch.\\n\\n**[2026-07-15 09:54] Diana**: Re-ran the CVE and CORS scans ahead of the release evidence pack — patch is still holding, no regressions since Bob's fix.\\n\\n**[2026-07-15 09:55] Bob**: Good. I'll note that in the security patch record.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 09 slack thread secur patch cor issu channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 07 10 last activ 2026 07 15 2026 07 10 14 20 diana bob i just ran a secur scan on the api we ve got a wide open cor polici access control allow origin is a no go for this project 2026 07 10 14 23 bob oop that wa left over from local test on the scaffold i ll tighten it up now 2026 07 10 14 43 bob appli the cor patch it now onli allow request from the defin allow _ origin in the environ config 2026 07 10 14 50 diana scan is come back clean now 2026 07 10 14 52 bob thank for the catch diana i ve ad a lint check to prevent from be commit in the futur 2026 07 1015 45 alic good catch let s make sure we don t have ani other dev onli flag leak into the main branch 2026 07 15 09 54 diana re ran the cve and cor scan ahead of the releas evid pack patch is still hold no regress sinc bob s fix 2026 07 15 09 55 bob good i ll note that in the secur patch record\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92a731a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-07-10-security-patch.md\", \"id\": \"19b85fe455718c06\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.26626203578877855, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07063783684111222, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7227185, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-07-10-security-patch.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e92a731a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-07-10-security-patch.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-07-10-security-patch.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 11