etadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e97f16a48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-17-Fix-Offset-Mismatch.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-17-Fix-Offset-Mismatch.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1109, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:20\", \"token_count\": 617, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-36\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-36\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-36\\n\\n**Title**: Multi-thread the local batch processing path\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-01\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd multi-threaded batch processing so local hardware can achieve higher throughput. The multi-thread batch path was integrated against the already-completed batch CLI tool, and the core multi-thread batch test passes.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-36\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-36\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-36\\n\\n**Title**: Multi-thread the local batch processing path\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-01\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Worker-pool-based multi-threading is integrated into the batch CLI pipeline.\\n\\n- Core multi-thread batch test passes against the completed batch CLI baseline.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-36\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-36\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-36\\n\\n**Title**: Multi-thread the local batch processing path\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-01\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd multi-threaded batch processing so local hardware can achieve higher throughput. The multi-thread batch path was integrated against the already-completed batch CLI tool, and the core multi-thread batch test passes.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-36\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-36\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-36\\n\\n**Title**: Multi-thread the local batch processing path\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-01\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-01**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because batch throughput needs multi-threading on local hardware.*\\n\\n- **2026-08-07**: Diana - Multi-thread Test Pass (Completed)\\n\\n - *Confirmed the core multi-thread batch test passes, integrated against the completed batch CLI.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 36 sourc id src cu ciph 36 task id ciph 36 titl multi thread the local batch process path status complet assigne charli prioriti normal date creat 2026 0801 descript add multi thread batch process so local hardwar can achiev higher throughput the multi thread batch path wa integr against the alreadi complet batch cli tool and the core multi thread batch test pass clickup task ciph 36 sourc id src cu ciph 36 task id ciph 36 titl multi thread the local batch process path status complet assigne charli prioriti normal date creat 2026 0801 accept criterion worker pool base multi thread is integr into the batch cli pipelin core multi thread batch test pass against the complet batch cli baselin clickup task ciph 36 sourc id src cu ciph 36 task id ciph 36 titl multi thread the local batch process path status complet assigne charli prioriti normal date creat 2026 0801 descript add multi thread batch process so local hardwar can achiev higher throughput the multi thread batch path wa integr against the alreadi complet batch cli tool and the core multi thread batch test pass clickup task ciph 36 sourc id src cu ciph 36 task id ciph 36 titl multi thread the local batch process path status complet assigne charli prioriti normal date creat 2026 0801 activ histori 2026 0801 alic task creat open open the task becaus batch throughput need multi thread on local hardwar 2026 08 07 diana multi thread test pas complet confirm the core multi thread batch test pass integr against the complet batch cli\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e986a3e28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-36-Multi-threading-for-Local-Processing.md\", \"id\": \"eba1afabe0f8e711\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2571646207543892, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.047405058220555955, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7466036, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-36-Multi-threading-for-Local-Processing.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e986a3e28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-36-Multi-threading-for-Local-Processing.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-36-Multi-threading-for-Local-Processing.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 958, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:16\", \"token_count\": 489, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-20\\n\\n# Performance Design: Multi-threading Page Processing\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2020\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-03\\n\\n## Work-Allocation Approach\\n\\nInstead of our initial multiprocessing (forking) model which consumed too much RAM per worker, we are moving to a ThreadPoolExecutor model within a single process. \\n\\n- **Allocation**: We allocate work at the **Page Level** rather than the Document Level. A 100-page PDF is split into 100 individual rendering tasks, which are distributed across 8 worker threads.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-20\\n\\n# Performance Design: Multi-threading Page Processing\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2020\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-03\\n\\n## Observed Bottleneck\\n\\nBecause the Python GIL (Global Interpreter Lock) restricts true parallel execution of Python bytecode, we expected a bottleneck. However, the actual bottleneck is in the `re2` C-extension during the pattern matching phase. When 8 threads simultaneously hit the regex engine with large text spans, lock contention inside the C-extension causes CPU cache trashing, dropping throughput by 15% compared to sequential processing for very dense text.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-20\\n\\n# Performance Design: Multi-threading Page Processing\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2020\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-03\\n\\n## The Trade-off\\n\\nWe are trading CPU efficiency for memory stability. Multi-threading allows us to keep only one copy of the 50MB PII Dictionary in RAM. If we used multiprocessing, a 16-core machine would need nearly 1GB just for the dictionary copies.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-20\\n\\n# Performance Design: Multi-threading Page Processing\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2020\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-03\\n\\n## Undecided: Safety Limits\\n\\nWe haven't finalized the `max_workers` cap for systems with high core counts (e.g., 32-core workstations). Should we cap the thread pool at 16 to prevent OS-level I/O starvation when writing the temporary BMPs to disk? We need a heavy I/O benchmark before hardcoding this limit.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 20 perform design multi thread page process owner charli document key doc 2020 last updat 2026 08 03 work alloc approach instead of our initi multiprocess fork model which consum too much ram per worker we are move to a threadpoolexecutor model within a singl process alloc we alloc work at the page level rather than the document level a100 page pdf is split into 100 individu render task which are distribut across 8 worker thread sourc id src gdoc 20 perform design multi thread page process owner charli document key doc 2020 last updat 2026 08 03 observ bottleneck becaus the python gil global interpret lock restrict true parallel execut of python bytecod we expect a bottleneck howev the actual bottleneck is in the re2 c extens dure the pattern match phase when 8 thread simultan hit the regex engin with larg text span lock content insid the c extens caus cpu cach trash drop throughput by 15 compar to sequenti process for veri dens text sourc id src gdoc 20 perform design multi thread page process owner charli document key doc 2020 last updat 2026 08 03 the trade off we are trade cpu effici for memori stabil multi thread allow u to keep onli one copi of the 50mb pii dictionari in ram if we use multiprocess a 16 core machin would need near 1gb just for the dictionari copi sourc id src gdoc 20 perform design multi thread page process owner charli document key doc 2020 last updat 2026 08 03 undecid safeti limit we haven t final the max _ worker cap for system with high core count e g 32 core workstat should we cap the thread pool at 16 to prevent o level i o starvat when write the temporari bmps to disk we need a heavi i o benchmark befor hardcod this limit\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9e120248a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-03-Multi-threading-for-Local-Processing-Review.md\", \"id\": \"45601daedf619af1\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2531666707679668, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05793951538280973, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7086967, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-03-Multi-threading-for-Local-Processing-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9e120248a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-03-Multi-threading-for-Local-Processing-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-03-Multi-threading-for-Local-Processing-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1578, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:00\", \"token_count\": 507, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Worker Management Decision\\n\\nRetrospective note on the concurrency block confirmed 2026-08-25. For large-scale redaction jobs, the batch API moved from a synchronous blocking loop to an `asyncio`-driven queue: a single producer walks the file system and pushes document tasks, while a fixed pool of async workers pulls from the queue and orchestrates I/O against the redaction engine, built on top of the already-completed multi-threaded worker pool (T026).\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Ordering & Race Risk\\n\\nBecause documents vary widely in size, workers finish out of order. When multiple workers append to the same shared results manifest concurrently, writes can interleave and corrupt the JSON structure.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Update: Confirmed I/O Race, Throughput Regression\\n\\nConcurrency testing on 2026-08-25 confirmed the race is real, not just theoretical: under concurrent load, the race condition measurably cuts batch throughput by roughly 10% compared to the expected async speedup, because workers end up retrying/serializing around the corrupted-write recovery path. This is now blocking further rollout of the async scheduler.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nT037 is **Blocked** on resolving the manifest-write race before the async scheduler can be considered production-ready; the throughput regression it causes depends directly on how the T026 worker pool's result-writing is serialized.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 worker manag decis retrospect note on the concurr block confirm 2026 08 25 for larg scale redact job the batch api move from a synchron block loop to an asyncio driven queue a singl produc walk the file system and push document task while a fix pool of async worker pull from the queue and orchestr i o against the redact engin built on top of the alreadi complet multi thread worker pool t026 sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 order race risk becaus document vari wide in size worker finish out of order when multipl worker append to the same share result manifest concurr write can interleav and corrupt the json structur sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 updat confirm i o race throughput regress concurr test on 2026 08 25 confirm the race is real not just theoret under concurr load the race condit measur cut batch throughput by rough 10 compar to the expect async speedup becaus worker end up retri serial around the corrupt write recoveri path this is now block further rollout of the async schedul sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 status t037 is block on resolv the manifest write race befor the async schedul can be consid product readi the throughput regress it caus depend direct on how the t026 worker pool s result write is serial\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9a578b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"id\": \"188f8e49d969781d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2529166807679668, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05793951538280973, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7078634, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9a578b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1694, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:51\", \"token_count\": 573, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-61\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Async Batch I/O Race\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-25\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 10:20] Diana**: Blocker on the async batch path. Under concurrent load the workers hit an I/O race and throughput drops — roughly 10% versus the sync baseline.\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 10:21] Bob**: Is that the scheduler shell or the workers we just added?\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 10:23] Diana**: The workers. Scheduler alone was fine; once concurrent workers share I/O with the existing multi-thread batch pool, the race shows up.\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 11:48] Charlie**: That pool is the multi-thread path. Mixing it with async workers without coordinating I/O was going to bite us.\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 12:50] Alice**: Then we stop here. I have to leave the async batch work blocked until the race with the multi-thread pool is sorted. A 10% hit is not shippable.\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 12:51] Bob**: Ok.\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 12:52] Bob**: Fair. I'll hold further async work until we understand the interaction with that pool.\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 12:54] Diana**: I'll capture the repro steps so we can re-run once there's a candidate fix.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 61 slack thread async batch i o race channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 25 2026 08 25 10 20 diana blocker on the async batch path under concurr load the worker hit an i o race and throughput drop rough 10 versus the sync baselin 2026 08 25 10 21 bob is that the schedul shell or the worker we just ad 2026 08 25 10 23 diana the worker schedul alon wa fine onc concurr worker share i o with the exist multi thread batch pool the race show up 2026 08 25 11 48 charli that pool is the multi thread path mix it with async worker without coordin i o wa go to bite u 2026 08 25 12 50 alic then we stop here i have to leav the async batch work block until the race with the multi thread pool is sort a 10 hit is not shippabl 2026 08 25 12 51 bob ok 2026 08 25 12 52 bob fair i ll hold further async work until we understand the interact with that pool 2026 08 25 12 54 diana i ll captur the repro step so we can re run onc there s a candid fix\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92db1c48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-25-async-batch-io-race.md\", \"id\": \"a9c09e16686f535a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24967762274760036, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.042137829639429074, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73393714, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-25-async-batch-io-race.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e92db1c48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-25-async-batch-io-race.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-25-async-batch-io-race.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1123, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:32\", \"token_count\": 349, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-35\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Benchmark Results\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-11\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 08:42] Evan**: The benchmark node finally got provisioned. Rerunning the scripts on real bare-metal hardware now instead of a stand-in.\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 08:44] Alice**: Good timing — glad that block is cleared.\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 08:47] Evan**: Full run is going. Should have results to share by tomorrow.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 10:17] Diana**: Results are in. Since the multi-threading work is already done, I used it as the baseline for comparison — the numbers line up with what we expected from that work.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:30] Alice**: Great. Are we publishing these as the official release figures?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:32] Diana**: Yes — publishing now. Calling this done; it depends on the multi-threading baseline.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc